---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  currentPath="/privacy/"
  title="Privacy | TRACED"
  description="How TRACED handles privacy: no accounts, analytics, or tracking cookies, and password checks hash locally in your browser."
  robots="noindex,follow"
>

  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="page">
    <header class="page-head band">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated October 21, 2026</p>
    </header>
    <div class="wrap">

      <article class="prose">
        <section>
          <h2>No accounts, cookies, or analytics</h2>
          <p>
            TRACED is a static site hosted on Cloudflare Pages. It doesn't have user accounts, analytics, tracking
            cookies, or user profiles.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Password checks</h2>
          <p>
            The password checker uses Have I Been Pwned's k-anonymity API. Your browser hashes the password locally
            with SHA-1, sends only the first 5 characters of that hash, and compares the returned list on your own
            device. Your password and its full hash never leave the browser.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Data sources</h2>
          <p>
            Case files are built from public Have I Been Pwned breach data. TRACED isn't affiliated with Have I Been
            Pwned or Troy Hunt.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Network requests</h2>
          <p>
            When you open a page, your browser downloads static files and breach metadata from Cloudflare Pages.
            Because all of the fonts are self-hosted on this domain, nothing calls out to Google Fonts or any ad or
            tracking scripts. If you run a password check, your browser makes one request to the Pwned Passwords API
            with that 5-character hash prefix.
          </p>
          <p>
            Cloudflare Pages and the Pwned Passwords API may still keep standard server request logs on their side, and
            I don't have control over those.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Browser storage</h2>
          <p>
            If you pick a theme or font in the Aa menu, TRACED saves that preference in your browser's local storage so
            it stays set on your next visit. That data stays on your device and never gets sent anywhere. You can wipe
            it anytime by clearing site data in your browser.
          </p>
          <p>
            TRACED doesn't store your searches or build any kind of profile. Your browser might still keep normal
            history, cached pages, or autofill entries depending on your own browser settings.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>What the archive can't tell you</h2>
          <p>
            Case files only summarize public breach records: when the breach happened, what kinds of data leaked, and
            whether passwords were exposed. They can't tell you whether your own email address or account was in a
            breach. To check that, use
            <a href="https://haveibeenpwned.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Have I Been Pwned<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
            directly.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            If you have questions about privacy or how this site works, you can reach me at
            <a href="https://jonathanrreed.com/contact/" rel="noopener">jonathanrreed.com/contact/</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
